WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:01.539
Whoa.

00:00:01.539 --> 00:00:02.539
Whoa.

00:00:02.539 --> 00:00:03.539
Whoa.

00:00:03.539 --> 00:00:06.760
Season 3 of Sunny Family Cult on CryptTV gets
crazy.

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:09.810
If you want to hear all the hidden details
about the big connection between Look-See

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:13.990
and Sunny Family Cult, then what you’re
gonna want to do is watch this whole video.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:15.839
From start to finish.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.240
This video is sponsored by CryptTV.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:26.770
Sunny Family Cult is back, and it picks up
right where Season 2 left off with Taylor

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:31.110
being driven into the desert… which confused
me a bit because I always thought they lived

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:34.680
in Iowa… there is actually an answer to
this question of how they end up in the desert,

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:39.930
in a now unlisted miniseries called Roger’s
Vlog, which takes place between Season 2 and

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:43.670
Season 3 and can only be found by looking
through the playlist section on Crypt’s

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:44.670
channel.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:45.670
Let’s check it out.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:49.940
“My dad won’t stop until he finds me.”

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:52.230
“Oh I believe that.

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.230
Absolutely.

00:00:53.230 --> 00:01:00.190
But luckily, we’ve got four states in between
him and us, so, we’re farther away from

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:01.790
Iowa than he’s ever been in his entire life.”

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:03.850
Which puts them California.

00:01:03.850 --> 00:01:08.350
Now Roger’s vlog doesn’t exactly go up
with Casey Neistat levels of consistency,

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:11.861
but we do get a little more information in
the second, and at the time of making this,

00:01:11.861 --> 00:01:12.861
final vlog.

00:01:12.861 --> 00:01:19.440
"When I started this cult about 20 years ago,
my brother didn’t realize the significance.

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:21.850
He didn’t see that there was a--”

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:26.479
“Can he see that you started the Sunny Family
Cult?”

00:01:26.479 --> 00:01:33.430
“People have been talking about Sunny Family
for like 30 years, since like, the 80s.

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:35.740
The town’s full of stories.”

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:40.370
“Yes, there was a cult back in the 80s,
but it was not the Sunny Family Cult that

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:41.549
I started.”

00:01:41.549 --> 00:01:45.460
This confirms what I predicted in my last
Things You Missed on Sunny Family Cult Season

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:49.689
1 and 2, about how Roger’s chapter of the
cult branches off of the original.

00:01:49.689 --> 00:01:53.340
So after driving halfway across the country,
they end up in the motel in the California

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:54.340
desert.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:57.430
But after attempting to escape and getting
a couple innocent people chopped up by Roger,

00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:00.000
Taylor finds herself tied up in the motel
room.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.770
“No more bringing chaos into the world to
show people what is really important, it’s

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:05.689
time to wipe it clean.

00:02:05.689 --> 00:02:07.650
Start over.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:09.520
Together.”

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:13.870
So as I mentioned before, Roger’s chapter
of the cult is the antithesis of Elias’s

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:17.680
chapter, and many of the flashback scenes
here in Season 3 show how that divide was

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:18.680
formed.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.959
This line really spells out exactly how the
two values differ.

00:02:20.959 --> 00:02:24.909
It’s mentioned from the very beginning how
the purpose of Elias’s cult is to introduce

00:02:24.909 --> 00:02:33.760
chaos and disrupt bonality, and in season
3 we get to see exactly why those values are

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:34.760
adopted.

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:38.400
Taylor of course, being someone who has grown
up learning the ways of Elias, is naturally

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.290
repulsed by Rodger’s ideas, and has this
to say about him.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:44.450
“You’re a monster.

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:46.609
No I’m not.

00:02:46.609 --> 00:02:50.219
I need you for that.”

00:02:50.219 --> 00:02:54.129
And that line leads us into the main plot
of this season, Roger’s conquest to fulfill

00:02:54.129 --> 00:02:56.489
the ritual from this ancient book he found.

00:02:56.489 --> 00:03:00.559
We get to see a little more of that book in
Episode 2, and it is filled with Things You

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:03.309
Missed.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:09.019
This is the first page that we get a good
look at, and a closer inspection reveals that

00:03:09.019 --> 00:03:10.529
it’s all about Look-See.

00:03:10.529 --> 00:03:16.360
The Latin text, “tempus edax rerum” translates
to “time, devourer of all things.”

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:20.180
That, of course ties into Look-See’s iconic
accessory, his stopwatch.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:24.689
There’s also a clock present on this page,
a sketch of Look-See’s hand and mouth and

00:03:24.689 --> 00:03:28.219
the act of Look-See taking a body part, in
this case, the face, from someone who was

00:03:28.219 --> 00:03:30.109
not able to release.

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:35.069
There’s also a much deeper possible connection
with Look-See that I’ll touch back on later

00:03:35.069 --> 00:03:36.159
in this video.

00:03:36.159 --> 00:03:40.129
The next page looks to be about Soot, the
newest CryptTV serialization, directed by

00:03:40.129 --> 00:03:42.680
my very talented friend, Danny Donahue.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:47.389
There’s only one episode of Soot out so
far, but the tagline is “Every Cycle must

00:03:47.389 --> 00:03:51.779
be completed,” and the episode seems to
compare cycles of electricity and life cycles.

00:03:51.779 --> 00:03:55.270
The Latin on the page to the right contains
the phrases, “he began to perish” and

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:59.870
“difficult for those in the highest…”
something, that’s where it cuts off.

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:03.510
The text also mentions something about selection,
and there is an image of a human eye.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:07.519
I’m sure we’ll find more about how all
that ties into the themes of the series very

00:04:07.519 --> 00:04:08.519
soon.

00:04:08.519 --> 00:04:11.999
The next page doesn’t have any legible text,
but it does contain the symbol of The Birch,

00:04:11.999 --> 00:04:17.260
the most popular short film on CryptTV, which
will also be serialized in the near future.

00:04:17.260 --> 00:04:22.730
There’s also page on the the cursed statue
from another recent Crypt series, Stoneheart.

00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:26.920
The Latin on the left page says something
about a sacred dance, thought I can’t make

00:04:26.920 --> 00:04:30.840
out much more than that, and the English on
the right reads: “For she, the protector,

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:34.220
will strike down all that oppose those that
would denounce her name.

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:37.860
When for the stones the man cast will break
the bones of his enemies.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:39.790
She seeks to redress that wrong.

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:42.870
Come to her and she will end all your pain.

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:45.590
All your…” and that’s where it cuts
off.

00:04:45.590 --> 00:04:49.410
The next page is a bit more ambiguous, but
it shows what appears to be Aponi, the main

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:51.900
witch from Stoneheart.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:54.890
And moreover, this is just a really cool illustration.

00:04:54.890 --> 00:04:57.880
Moving on, the symbols on the left here are
not anything that I’m familiar with, but

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:01.380
if anyone has any leads on how to decipher
them, please let me know in the comments.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:04.700
I’m sure you’re all familiar with the
Sunny Family Cult symbol, but what you may

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:08.760
have missed is when Roger moves his hand,
the shadow of another new creature can be

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:13.630
seen very briefly, before Roger turns the
page once again, and this is an important

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:17.420
one, because it details the ritual that becomes
the centerpiece of everything Roger is aiming

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:19.680
for in this season of Sunny Fam.

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:23.690
The whole reason Roger kidnaps Taylor, is
because he believes she is the one who can

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:26.230
help him unlock this hidden power.

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:30.910
She is the girl of 17 with violence etched
into her soul, with dark hair and dark eyes

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:35.780
pictured at the center here in this book,
and these monsters drawn above, Aponi, Mordeo

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:39.880
and Look-See, all existing Crypt creatures,
are examples of what kind of monsters might

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:42.170
be created from carrying out this ritual.

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:46.570
The diagram outlines 5 sacrifices and the
caption calls for: “a blood sacrifice of

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:49.360
four victims, and the fifth will become something.”

00:05:49.360 --> 00:05:54.110
The other side details what I can only imagine
is the transformation process from man to

00:05:54.110 --> 00:05:55.110
monster.

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:58.610
So after taking all of these pages in, Roger
looks up and see a vision of this girl.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:01.710
This shot is very reminiscent of an image
from one of the lesser known Crypt short films,

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:05.520
The Woman In The Book, where not much background
is given about the story, but a similar looking

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:09.080
creepy lady seems to be summoned from a book
in that short as well.

00:06:09.080 --> 00:06:13.490
Mr. Sandman also features a similar book,
so the idea of Crypt lore being hidden in

00:06:13.490 --> 00:06:17.240
ancient texts has been established even before
Sunny Family Cult.

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:21.500
Now at this point, at the end of this second
episode of Season 3, you could chalk up all

00:06:21.500 --> 00:06:26.010
of these references to other CryptTV properties
to be nothing more than fun easter eggs, but

00:06:26.010 --> 00:06:30.360
going forward into episode 3, it becomes very
clear that all of these worlds are destined

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:32.900
to collide in Sunny Family Cult.

00:06:38.860 --> 00:06:44.000
If you’re enjoying the video so far, you’ve
probably noticed this stylish attire.

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:48.450
If you want to be part of the Sunny Fam, you’ve
got to have this merch.

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:49.870
And there’s only one way to get it.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:53.750
All you have to do sign up for the Crypt newsletter
using the link in the description, and you’ll

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:57.110
be in the know about their exclusive monthly
merch drops.

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:59.140
Now back to Things You Missed.

00:07:02.080 --> 00:07:05.950
Remember back in Season 2, when Taylor and
Jaina are being chased by the masked Roger,

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:09.560
and Taylor asks Jaina, if she can see him
too, basically suggesting that she’s been

00:07:09.560 --> 00:07:10.560
having hallucinations?

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:11.990
“You see him too?

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:16.430
What if those visions tie into Taylor’s
status as the chosen girl in the prophecy

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:17.530
of Roger’s book?

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:20.750
The third episode begins with a pair of hands
that should be familiar to anyone who’s

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:23.100
seen Look-See, attacking Taylor in her sleep.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:27.660
She wakes up back in her room, where she sees
yet another monster rise up before her.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:30.300
Based on the shadow on the wall, it looks
like Aponi.

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:32.280
But this is also just a dream.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:36.450
As this episode progresses, it becomes more
and more clear that these are more than just

00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:37.450
references.

00:07:37.450 --> 00:07:41.940
Sunny Family Cult is the epicenter of a CryptTV
cinematic universe including all of their

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:43.030
monster properties.

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:46.910
The hastag, #MonsterWithin is more than just
a catchy tagline.

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:51.250
In this Crypt Universe, there’s a monster
within all of us, waiting to be unleashed

00:07:51.250 --> 00:07:52.810
by this ancient ritual.

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:54.210
Roger is buying all into it.

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:58.250
He’s gone and got a tattoo with the Sunny
Family Cult logo at the center, the cursed

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:02.040
statue from Stoneheart, Look-See, Soot, and
the stick symbol from the Birch.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:06.490
All of these icons have risen up from the
girl making the final sacrifice.

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:10.120
As Roger tries to convince Taylor to take
part, he tells her the following.

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:12.860
“We can do this together.

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:16.382
We can wipe away what we hate in this world.”

00:08:16.382 --> 00:08:20.790
This is an interesting take because Roger
believes he is the good guy, and in the end,

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:21.790
he might be.

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:26.440
Look-See, Mordeo, Aponi, The Birch… all
of their victims tend to be criminals, bad

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:29.170
people or people with dangerous flaws.

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:35.880
“If that’s what you call a monster, then
yes.

00:08:35.889 --> 00:08:39.740
We will turn ourselves into monsters.”

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:45.180
Taylor, of course, thinks this is insane,
and gets the heck out of there, taking refuge

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:47.050
in the motel manager’s office.

00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:49.629
Unfortunately for her, Roger has been there
already.

00:08:49.629 --> 00:08:50.860
For those of you keeping count at home…

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:54.420
I know one of you is…  that’s 3 kills at the motel.

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:57.809
Taylor uses his fingerprint to unlock his
phone and call her dad, who by the way has

00:08:57.809 --> 00:08:59.259
a North Carolina area code.

00:08:59.259 --> 00:09:03.769
I guess what Roger said about him never having
ventured this far from Iowa is still true.

00:09:03.769 --> 00:09:07.340
That is… until episode 4, the season finale

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:17.250
It is at the this point, that we finally see
the face of the girl from Rodger’s visions,

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:19.379
and it looks exactly like Taylor.

00:09:19.379 --> 00:09:22.130
A rush of images flash on screen very quickly.

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:22.880
Look-See.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:23.920
The cursed statue from Stoneheart.

00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:24.580
Troubled Youth.

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:25.120
Soot.

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:25.720
Mordeo.

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:26.460
Aponi.

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:28.020
And the famous monster from The Birch.

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:32.720
Taylor’s Dad showing up, ends up working
in Roger’s favor, because he unknowingly

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:34.870
becomes the fourth sacrifice at the motel.

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:40.430
It is as it is written in the book: four blood
sacrifices and the fifth will become something.

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:45.080
Taylor’s anger gets the better of her, and
she gives Roger exactly what he wants, making

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:51.000
him the fifth sacrifice and ending the season
on his revival.

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:04.120
I’m excited to see whatever monster Roger
becomes in the next season.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:08.339
Because whatever it is really becomes the
biggest boss in all of CryptTV canon.

00:10:08.339 --> 00:10:13.689
The bad guy that presides over all other bad
guys on the Crypt channel.

00:10:13.689 --> 00:10:17.769
The one that brings each series together…
into one.

00:10:17.769 --> 00:10:22.529
This is a really exciting time to be a follower
of the  Sunny Family Cult and the Crypt channel

00:10:22.529 --> 00:10:23.529
in general.

00:10:23.529 --> 00:10:27.019
There are series within this cinematic universe
airing right now, and you don’t want to

00:10:27.019 --> 00:10:31.709
miss out, so make sure you subscribe to CryptTV
for scary episodes every Tuesday, Thursday

00:10:31.709 --> 00:10:35.040
and Friday and I’ll see you in the next
one.

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:37.399
Assuming we both survive.

